.TH PANEL 1 "October 2026" "ServerPanel 1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
panel \- terminal administration panel for Debian 13
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo panel
.br
.B panel motd
.br
.B panel --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B panel
is a keyboard-first terminal interface for systemd services, Apache
VirtualHosts and host metrics. Interactive administration requires root.
No web interface or extra network port is required.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B LEFT / RIGHT
Switch section; move between the actions of the selected item.
.TP
.B UP / DOWN
Select a service, site or action.
.TP
.B ENTER
Focus the action pane, then run the selected action.
.TP
.B TAB
Move focus between the list and the actions.
.TP
.B 1 / 2 / 3
Jump to SERVICES, VPS or SITES.
.TP
.B ESC
Return to the list or close a dialog.
.TP
.B N
Create a service or site, depending on the section.
.TP
.B A
Show all systemd units or only the followed ones.
.TP
.B R
Refresh inventories and metrics.
.TP
.B Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/serverpanel/config.json
.br
.I /etc/update-motd.d/85-serverpanel
.br
.I /etc/systemd/system/panel-*.service
.br
.I /etc/apache2/sites-available/panel-*.conf
.SH SECURITY
Application processes run under dedicated unprivileged system users.
No administrative command is executed via a shell. Critical networking/SSH
units are protected from stop/disable operations. Use the system console for
emergency maintenance. Always back up the server before large changes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR apache2ctl (8),
.BR certbot (7),
.BR journalctl (1)
